commit 7fc75b566ef51a70825cf429ffee433498961f06
Author: aldiss <v.drobkov@gmail.com>
Date:   Fri Jul 31 20:22:07 2026 +0200

    ask_user receipt: preserve authenticated-dismiss actor (dl-13527)
    
    deriveReceipt gated the responder author on answer-presence
    (`answerPresent && response.author`), so an authenticated dashboard DISMISS —
    which the browser gateway server-stamps with the operator author but carries no
    answer — had its dismisser identity DROPPED. A dismiss is a real operator action;
    losing WHO dismissed is the bug.
    
    Redefine `author` = the RESPONDER actor: whoever ANSWERED **or**
    authenticated-DISMISSED. Preserve the responder-stamped author whenever present
    (`if (response.author)`), independent of answer-presence. `renderedBy` stays
    separate (the RENDERER). The render identity still never leaks into `author`:
    respond() sets `author: response.author` (responder-only), cancel() sets none, and
    the render author lives in entry.renderedAuthor → renderedBy — so
    operator-render→TUI-answer/cancel still yields no author (regression-guarded).
    
    `answered` is unchanged (`!cancelled && answerPresent`), so a dismiss with an
    author is still `answered:false`; an operator ANSWER remains
    `answered && author.isOperator`, and ask-user-tool still gates "User responded" on
    `receipt.answered` — a dismiss never reads as a response.
    
    Also correct two stale doc-comments (code was already right): the render-ACK
    author threads into receipt.renderedBy, not receipt.author
    (protocol.ts PromptRenderedServerMessage, browser-gateway.ts prompt_rendered).
    
    Adds RED→GREEN tests: authenticated dashboard dismiss preserves author (+ distinct
    dismisser vs renderer), TUI cancel authorless, bus timeout authorless + renderedBy,
    operator-render→TUI-answer regression guard, and the full PromptBus.respond()
    cancelled+authored path.

